    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d181">

                <pb facs="0329" n="237" sameAs="frus:frus1899/pg237"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Hart to Mr.
                            Hay</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States of America</hi>,<lb/><hi
                                rendition="#italic">Bogota</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1898-11-07"><hi rendition="#italic">November
                                7, 1898</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 119.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge the receipt
                    of your telegram of November 1, which I translate as follows: <quote
                        rend="blockquote">
                        <p>Proceed with demand Star and Herald claim. This Government imperatively
                            insists on prompt payment.</p>
                        <p rendition="#right"><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hill.</hi></p>
                    </quote>
                </p>
                <p>Owing to the disturbed condition of affairs, as reported in my No. 120 of this
                    date, it has not been practicable to do business with the Government. I expect
                    to have an interview with the minister for foreign affairs this afternoon, when
                    of course the matter will be brought to a head and the Department will be at
                    once advised by cable.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Chas. Burdett
                    Hart</hi>.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
